WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.980
- It's complicated.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.250
That's a description that
applies to a lot of activity

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.200
in and around Washington these days,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.440
but especially applies to
one of the most important

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.300
relationships President
Joe Biden is working on.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.300
His long acquaintance

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.080
with Israeli prime minister,
Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.390
These two leaders have been
joined anew in recent days

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.760
of course, by the rising
tensions between Israelis

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.960
and Palestinians and specifically
the outbreak of violence

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.360
between Israel and Hamas
forces in the Gaza Strip.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.330
President Biden and
Prime Minister Netanyahu,

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.660
have talked numerous times
during the course of this crisis.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.800
And publicly Mr. Biden has
largely defended Israel's right

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.630
to respond with military
force to Hamas rocket attacks

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.194
saying, "It was entitled
to act in self defense."

00:00:41.194 --> 00:00:43.800
- The United States fully
supports Israel's right

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.220
to defend itself against
indiscriminate rocket attacks

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.040
from Hamas and other Gaza
based terrorist groups

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.440
that have taken the lives of
innocent civilians in Israel.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.450
- Privately he reportedly
has been much tougher

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.430
with Mr. Netanyahu, saying,
"He expected him to deescalate

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:01.840
the situation and deal with
Palestinian grievances."

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.040
His nudging may have led to the ceasefire

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.350
that's finally taken hold but these two

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.120
are far from done with each other.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.810
Now the Biden administration
inevitably will be deeply

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.140
involved in trying to
broker a broader agreement

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.360
to simultaneously deal with
Israel's security concerns,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.340
as well as Palestinian simmering anger

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.410
at the way they're treated
by Israel, not just in Gaza,

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.380
but also in the West Bank and Jerusalem,

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.460
and increasingly inside Israel itself.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.050
The long history of this
relationship shows President Biden

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.010
is prepared to push Prime
Minister Netanyahu to go further

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.260
than he wants to accommodate
Palestinian demands.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.690
But also that he's more
likely to do his hard pressing

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.260
privately rather than publicly.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.430
- I don't talk about what
I tell people in private.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.830
I don't talk about what
we negotiate in private.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.010
- [Narrator] These two
men have known each other

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.560
since the early 1980s

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.740
when Mr. Netanyahu was
the second in charge

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.600
at the Israeli embassy in Washington,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.950
and then later Israel's
ambassador to the United nations.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.250
Mr. Biden meanwhile was a US Senator

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.820
developing a particular
interest in foreign affairs.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.230
They came into closer contact in the 1990s

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.320
when Mr. Netanyahu became prime minister

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.700
and Senator Biden was
on his way to becoming

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.080
the top Democrat and eventually chairman

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.680
of the Senate Foreign Relations Committee.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.390
They were in these positions
of power in the early 2000s

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.600
when the George W. Bush
administration was both marshaling

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.880
an international response to
the 9/11 terrorist attacks

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.660
and also trying to get peace talks going

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.210
between Israel and the Palestinians.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.010
Their relationship became more important

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.950
during the Obama administration

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.980
when Mr. Biden was vice-president

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.370
and Mr. Netanyahu again
became prime minister.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.290
Their relationship also became
more tense in those days.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.280
The Obama administration
put a high priority

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.740
on finding a new Israeli
Palestinian peace accord.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.050
Vice-president Biden was
visiting Israel in March, 2010,

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.110
trying to assure Israel of
American support for its security

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.560
in any such peace deal

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.220
when the Netanyahu administration
announced the construction

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.620
of hundreds of new housing units
for Jews in East Jerusalem,

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.900
the part of the city where
Palestinians envisioned

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.070
putting the capital of a
Palestinian state someday.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.400
Israeli housing there is one
of the most sensitive issues

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.680
for Palestinians and one that
US officials have long thought

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.170
undermines the chances for diplomacy.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.230
Mr. Biden was blindsided
and he wasn't happy.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.490
There were tensions again
on another front in 2015,

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.970
when Prime Minister
Netanyahu visited Washington,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.200
and at the invitation
of Republican leaders

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.580
delivered a speech to a
joint session of Congress

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.310
devoted to attacking the Iran Nuclear Deal

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.440
the Obama administration
was then negotiating.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.660
- The greatest danger facing our world

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:39.180
is the marriage of militant
Islam with nuclear weapons.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.420
To defeat ISIS and let
Iran get nuclear weapons

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.740
would be to win the
battle, but lose the war.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.750
We can't let that happen.
(crowd clapping)

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.010
- [Narrator] Obama administration
officials were furious

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.690
and vice-president Biden who
normally would have attended

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.640
such a speech was notably absent.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.560
Through these tensions,

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.770
President Biden and
Prime Minister Netanyahu

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.080
appear to have maintained
a good relationship,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.360
one in which they are generally
supportive of each other

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.260
publicly, but have blunt
and sometimes acrimonious

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.130
conversations in private.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.340
Mr. Biden in particular
seems to have decided

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.290
to avoid the public sparring

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.920
that hurt president Obama's
relationship with Israel.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.910
These two men are now being tested anew,

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.930
as it is it may be that their
relationship is shored up

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.200
by one characteristic that they share.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.530
Both Joe Biden and Benjamin Netanyahu

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.064
are very good at the art
of political survival.

00:04:32.064 --> 00:04:35.314
(soft dramatic music)

